A5 removes the home venue and delegated cake arrangement that enable that entrance.\",\n        \"cardContribution\": \"A trusts B as a personal anchor but silently conditions delegated control on the mascot remaining absent.\",\n        \"sameGameHeightened\": \"A5 acts on the condition by reclaiming planning while still asking the trusted person to accompany A.\"\n      },\n      \"reservation\": \"A3's reassurance could respond to the small guest count alone; the mascot condition becomes fully legible retrospectively through A5. The trust reversal concerns planning, not all companionship. No rewrite is needed.\",\n      \"alternativeComparison\": \"The preserved alternative explicitly retrieves a key and then restores conditional access. This alternative keeps the condition private and preserves companionship through a quieter change of plan.\",\n      \"accept\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"exampleId\": \"S230-single-b\",\n      \"candidateHash\": \"d9890fa235ba4f4233436c984be301eaee67a61d0c48048324c17c862575c749\",\n      \"secondPass\": {\n        \"ratings\": {\n          \"cardFidelity\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"A1 honors the photographed boy's vow, A3 knowingly accepts being his 'traitor,' and A5 restores match attendance while inviting that earlier self's judgment.\"\n          },\n          \"responseLogic\": {\n            \"score\": 5,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2's doubled pay motivates A3's mortgage justification. B4 proposes canceling the season ticket, directly causing A5 to retain it and commit to weekly return trips.\"\n          },\n          \"relationship\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B2 has booked the van and B4 manages the ticket cancellation; A3's 'our mortgage' gives B a shared practical stake in the move.\"\n          },\n          \"heightening\": {\n            \"score\": 4,\n            \"evidence\": \"B4 makes the sporting part of the old vow materially vulnerable, so